# Copy to .env.local for development, or set these in your host's secret manager.
# Values here are placeholders only. Never commit real credentials.

# --- Discord presence (public identifier, not a credential) -------------------
# Your numeric Discord user ID. The account must also be tracked by Lanyard
# (join https://discord.gg/UrXF2cfJ7F). See README for exact steps.
DISCORD_USER_ID=

# --- ListenBrainz ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Simplest and safest: just your ListenBrainz username. Public listens need no
# token, so there is nothing secret to leak.
# The name in your profile address (listenbrainz.org/user/<name>). Not sure how it is
# spelled? List several, separated by commas: the first one ListenBrainz knows is used.
LISTENBRAINZ_USERNAME=
# Optional: a user token from https://listenbrainz.org/settings/ . Used only on the
# server, once, to ask ListenBrainz whose token it is (a valid one decides the
# account). Keep it out of the repo, the browser and logs. Not needed if
# LISTENBRAINZ_USERNAME is set; if the token is rejected the username is used.
LISTENBRAINZ_TOKEN=

# --- GitHub (server-side only) ------------------------------------------------
# Fine-grained personal access token limited to "Public repositories (read-only)"
# with no additional permissions. Optional but recommended: raises GitHub's rate limit
# (shared hosts exhaust the 60 anonymous requests an hour) and enables the GraphQL calendar.
# Without it the calendar uses GitHub's public contributions graph.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Troubleshooting ------------------------------------------------------------
# 1 = show owner-only hints inside the panels and serve /status (anyone who knows the
# address can read it while it is on, so remove it when everything works). 0 = never.
# Unset = on in `npm run dev`, off in a production build.
# Run `npm run doctor` for a connectivity report.
SHOW_DIAGNOSTICS=

# --- Link previews -------------------------------------------------------------
# The public address of the site, e.g. https://example.com. Recommended on every host
# except Vercel (detected automatically).
# SITE_URL=

# --- Discord profile fallbacks (owner-supplied, not live Discord fields) ------
# Lanyard does not relay a Discord banner or "About Me". The site reads them from
# your Lanyard KV keys "bio" and "banner" (see README). These two are only the
# last-resort fallbacks if KV is empty. PROFILE_BANNER_URL must be https://.
PROFILE_BANNER_URL=
PROFILE_BIO=
